# Negative control — a Module Group is gated on the host slot's OWN accept
# list again, reversing F2 (design.md §D4/§D6, tasks.md 2.0 F2 — board rule 2
# makes the group universal; only its MEMBERS are checked against the host
# slot, never the group itself). Pairs with F2: after the real fix, a group
# must NOT be rejected by this gate anywhere, because no accept list carries
# the `group` tag any more (F2 also removed it from all 16 rows).
#
# Reproduced by direct execution before filing: a group placed in
# `utility.top` — a slot the fixed resolver admits unconditionally — resolves
# to `{ status: "rejected", reason: 'utility.top does not accept a module
# group.' }` once this patch is applied, instead of `{ status: "group", ... }`
# with its member resolved on its own merits.
#
# Intended RED: any assertion that a group renders (status "group") in a slot
# whose accept list does not name `group` — which, after F2, is every slot.
#
# REGENERATED 2026-08-24. The previous hunk targeted resolveSlotAssignment but Task 5
# added resolveContentSlotAssignment with an IDENTICAL isModuleGroupRef branch shape,
# so git apply fuzzy-matched it into the wrong function: it still applied, still went
# red, and reddened two unrelated tests while resolve.test.ts's group tests — its
# actual target — stayed green. A control that grades the wrong thing while looking
# healthy is worse than one that fails to apply, because failure is loud.
